{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A greedy edge colouring of any graph, parallel edges and self-loops included, with at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2Δ − 1 colours: rustworkx "},{"code":"graph_greedy_edge_color","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the largest-first colouring of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line graph, with the same colours. Edges by the number of other edges they share an end"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with, most first (a parallel copy counts at both ends, a self-loop meets each other edge at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its vertex once), ties in position order; each takes the least colour of no edge it shares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an end with that is already coloured. A self-loop is one edge at its vertex, as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"isEdgeColoring(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n + m · Δ) time, O(n + m) memory, without building the line graph."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"greedyEdgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeColoring","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/EdgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyEdgeColoring()"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedyedgecoloring()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["d